WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.210
Antarctica's Dry Valleys.

2
00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:07.670
The mean annual air temperature is
about minus 19.8 degrees Celsius.

3
00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:12.710
At the base of the glaciers there,
it is about minus 17 degrees Celsius.

4
00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:15.290
The ice is frozen to the rock.

5
00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:17.630
These glaciers barely move.

6
00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:21.630
Yet elsewhere, ice can race
forward metres in a day.

7
00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:25.830
All glaciers creep, as ice
deforms under its own weight.

8
00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:29.530
So why do some race,
while others hardly shift?

9
00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:31.850
In this mission, you'll
look under the ice,

10
00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:35.270
at what happens where a
glacier meets its bed.

11
00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:38.450
Then you'll compare how fast
ice moves at different depths,

12
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:42.870
and test your ideas on glaciers
in very different climates.

13
00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:46.310
Your mission: explain why
some glaciers race forward,

14
00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:48.430
while others barely creep.
